# Push only after a green build

When the user asks to push, or when shipping code to origin:

1. Run `npm run build` and wait for it to succeed. Do not push a failing build.
2. Commit any remaining uncommitted work (including fixes found during the build) using the git commit protocol.
3. Then push to the tracked remote.

Do not skip the build to save time. If the build fails, fix it, rebuild, and only then commit and push.
